Adapted portions, taken from its references/five-fold-evaluation.md:

  - The four design questions of the auditor (over-engineering,
    side-effects, user QoL, shrinkability), in
    .claude/agents/gentle-ai-auditor.md, step 5.
  - The three cost axes (system, user, product) and the package of reasons
    for and against that the human decides with, in SKILL.md, step 10.

Changes made to the adapted material:

  - Reworded from the review of a pull request to the audit of a frozen
    contribution candidate, which may be an issue or a comment and not only
    a diff.
  - The first of its five questions (problem-solution fit) was not taken;
    this skill covers that ground with task-contract acceptance coverage.
  - The questions are recorded as structured `designCoverage` rows and
    `maintainerDecisions` in the auditor result, instead of prose, and the
    package is assembled by a controller from those rows rather than written
    by the reviewer.
  - English only; the original is bilingual (English and Spanish).

Everything else in this work is original to it.

Public edition: personal example paths and internal observation identifiers have been replaced. Runtime data and private history are excluded.
